@@ -5,8 +5,24 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 ## Status
 
 - Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list.
-- `/dashboard` shows the current user and the team.
-- There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet.
+- Authentication is WorkOS AuthKit: email + password and Google sign-in via the hosted
+  AuthKit screens. A WorkOS identity is linked to a Notely user by email on first sign-in.
+- `/dashboard` requires sign-in (enforced in `src/proxy.ts` and in the page itself).
+- There is no billing and no email yet.
+
+## Auth setup
+
+1. Create a WorkOS project at https://dashboard.workos.com.
+2. Under **Authentication**, enable **Email + Password** and **Google OAuth**
+   (WorkOS provides test Google credentials in the staging environment; use your own
+   Google OAuth client in production).
+3. Under **Redirects**, add `http://localhost:3000/auth/callback` as a redirect URI,
+   and set the sign-out redirect to `http://localhost:3000/`.
+4. `cp .env.example .env.local` and fill in the client ID, API key, and a 32+ char
+   cookie password (`openssl rand -base64 32`).
+
+Routes: `/sign-in`, `/sign-up` (redirect to AuthKit), `/auth/callback` (session
+exchange), sign out is a server action on the dashboard.
 
